 ("P4-090","AtmKIdmLLQ8",495,570,"review/hindsight","A roster or draft decision should be evaluated using information available before the match, rather than its observed outcome alone.","method","Roster selection commentary","high","low","Distinct from actual claim that any specific roster choice was correct."),
 ("P4-091","ijlmDdVIdtk",70,155,"composition/aggro_balance","He frames a contemporary Winston double-flex composition as multiple splits balancing attention: the pressured split yields, the others press, and high-level fights may repeat this exchange over several turns.","framework","2026 team-composition analysis","high","high","Terminology and composition are era dependent; compare 2023 split-core account."),
 ("P4-092","ijlmDdVIdtk",770,900,"bait/counterplay","Offering a punishable teammate can steer an opponent's decision but may cost a death; teams can adapt by declining the bait and conceding some space, with different subsequent risks.","case_judgment","Dallas Fuel–SSG review","medium","high","He explicitly leaves which style is better unresolved."),
 ("P4-093","prUv2eNrGD0",1020,1205,"hitscan/development","Across a small matched-map Sojourn sample, he observes progression in pre-fight poke, changing angles, scouting rotations, farming rail, and looking quickly for picks; the comparison is illustrative, not a controlled rank study.","observational_pattern","Five selected players from Diamond to pro","high","high","Guest speech is present; this row paraphrases the narrator's comparisons."),
 ("P4-094","prUv2eNrGD0",1460,1550,"hitscan/decision","The pro player describes farming rail from the tank and quickly scanning for exposed targets; the narrator highlights the speed of that transition as a higher-level distinction.","observational_pattern","Sojourn pro interview; narrator interpretation plus guest report","medium","high","Preserve speaker attribution; check footage for each alleged opportunity."),
 ("P4-095","N5fHwbNE-SQ",245,330,"bait/space","In a slow defensive style, the front line must actively delay an enemy walk-up while the backline keeps useful angles; standing very far back without contesting the path is insufficient.","conditional_rule","Cjay interview; speaker attribution needs audio check","low","high","Auto captions are heavily corrupted in this upload; do not promote without audio."),
 ("P4-096","iLX7uqsC1jE",750,780,"mechanics/close_fights","He cautions that mechanical differences and missed shots can decide otherwise sound fight plans, especially when a close match has small margins.","qualified_thesis","Q&A; illustrative estimate, not a measured 5% effect","high","low","Avoid a false dichotomy between mechanics and strategic understanding."),
 ("P4-097","iLX7uqsC1jE",1110,1145,"learning/attention","For a player unsure of their job, he advises writing a short list of possible duties and practicing one or two at a time to preserve awareness and flexibility.","method","Q&A advice","high","low","Specific three-to-four-item list suggested in speech."),
 ("P4-098","iLX7uqsC1jE",1180,1260,"learning/practice","Knowing a principle in theory is different from executing it; repeated practice of small, specific actions is needed to close that gap.","method","Q&A response to player frustration","high","low","The hundreds/thousands language is rhetorical, not a calibrated repetition count."),
 ("P4-099","x2jNJeKiMUU",985,1065,"game_design/counterplay","In a pre-release hero reaction, he worries that complete invulnerability on a flanker could remove too much opponent counterplay, while also valuing a flanker able to poke and later threaten the backline.","design_opinion","Speculative first impression of announced hero kit","medium","high","Do not treat predicted balance or kit behavior as a tested strategic fact."),
 ("P4-100","c92ESPjlveI",810,985,"turns/advantage","After gaining a brawl advantage, a slow push can preserve movement and defensive cooldowns while taking angles, so the team can bait an opponent's third or fourth turn without losing a trade.","conditional_rule","Late midfight brawl example","high","high","Extends first/second turn vocabulary into multi-cycle fights; exact ult and trade outcomes await visual review."),
 ("P4-101","JM50b3IU6-c",190,320,"composition/off_angle","A solo off angle benefits from mobility to find new sight lines and escape, burst to threaten immediately on a peek, and sustain or a health pack to resist being marked.","conditional_rule","2023 split composition and named hero examples","high","medium","Hero balance is era-specific; the selection criteria are more general than the names."),
 ("P4-102","JM50b3IU6-c",270,395,"composition/core","The tank core can occupy, threaten objective, and punish pursuit of the off angle while allowing the weaker off angle to create initial value before it commits its own resources.","mechanism","Split composition; patient setup","high","high","Actual geometry and objective trade depend on footage."),
 ("P4-103","JM50b3IU6-c",420,480,"space/danger","His 'red zone' is the opponent's immediate engage reach and the preceding 'yellow zone' requires caution; an off-angle player should react before that zone reaches them, using sound and scouting rather than waiting for visual confirmation.","definition","Close-map rush matchup; zone sizes approximate","high","high","Metaphoric zones, not calibrated distances. Audio and exact map distance should be checked."),
 ("P4-104","JM50b3IU6-c",610,790,"composition/split_distance","A split must remain close enough for the untouched core to punish an enemy push on the other; separating so far that this counterpressure arrives late defeats the setup.","conditional_rule","Toronto–Washington 4–1 to 3–2 example","high","high","Video required for claimed inter-core distances and fight outcome."),
 ("P4-105","JM50b3IU6-c",800,915,"composition/retake","After losing a fight, a split composition should restage its two angles rather than retake as a five-player stack; the more vulnerable off angle may need to set first.","conditional_rule","Flashpoint retake illustration","high","high","Objective percentage and trade value are his match interpretation."),
 ("P4-106","JM50b3IU6-c",925,1065,"composition/counterplay","Against a split composition, decide which core is beatable and how to occupy the other long enough to attack it; a simple five-player rush at one core can be punished from the second angle.","framework","Non-mirror counterplay, 2023 example","high","high","Specific 2v2/3v3 allocations remain matchup-dependent."),
 ("P4-107","JM50b3IU6-c",1260,1545,"composition/communication","A split can call which group must retreat and which can advance based on where the opponent commits; communicating enemy counts helps the distant core respond before it can see the threat itself.","conditional_rule","Second Toronto–Washington fight and mirror discussion","high","high","Overlaps P4-003 conceptually, but adds a scouting and communication trigger."),
 ("P4-108","z9n-JNB52rk",204,330,"support/positioning","A backline needs a position that can threaten an advancing tank while remaining hard for that tank to reach; excessive safety can remove the pressure that makes the position useful.","conditional_rule","Corner and tank–backline reach examples","high","high","The exact safe offset and threatened targets require map review."),
 ("P4-109","z9n-JNB52rk",606,735,"turns/cooldowns","Going first may mean using cooldowns to force a response without walking into the opponent's reach; a team can spend first and still plan to withdraw or punish the reply.","distinction","Corner neutral example, 2024","high","high","Refines P4-014's engage language; exact cooldown exchange awaits footage."),
 ("P4-110","z9n-JNB52rk",735,840,"space/corner","When both teams are held at a corner with little safe room to yield, the neutral can persist until a matchup, cooldown, angle, or other advantage changes the interaction.","case_judgment","Specific corner geometry; not a universal stalemate rule","medium","high","Speaker's geometric interpretation needs visual inspection."),
 ("P4-111","pMPwEwNEiQA",182,335,"genji/exit","A Genji taking enemy attention should plan an exit and an ally position to return to, preserving or sequencing wall climb, Deflect, and dash around that route.","conditional_rule","Genji replay review","high","high","Cooldown availability and route need POV validation."),
 ("P4-112","pMPwEwNEiQA",696,825,"genji/ultimate","A blade attempt becomes more favorable when opposing vulnerable players move into reachable range; using it solely because it is available can surrender the safer neutral pressure Genji already has.","conditional_rule","Specific blade decision in match review","medium","high","The target reach and fight result are the speaker's assessment."),
 ("P4-113","pMPwEwNEiQA",823,950,"genji/anticipation","A Genji on an angle should leave as enemy supports walk up into a punish setup, before the ultimate animation or damage makes the danger unmistakable.","conditional_rule","Specific support walk-up and Genji escape timing","high","high","The telegraph and whether retreat was possible require POV review."),
 ("P4-114","p609brPyPzg",303,456,"hazard/targeting","Hazard should reserve his movement engage for a vulnerable squishy who has moved beyond safety, rather than spend it on a tank who may be baiting; approaching can itself clear space.","conditional_rule","Early Hazard guide in 2024 matchup","medium","high","Hero mechanics and implied damage are patch dependent; inspect clip before treating combo as lethal."),
 ("P4-115","p609brPyPzg",455,647,"hazard/rotation","A Hazard staging near a likely backline rotation wants a position that is hard to scout or clear before the rotation, while close enough to punish the crossing.","conditional_rule","Map-specific ledge and high-ground examples","high","high","Proposed route denial requires map and POV review."),
 ("P4-116","p609brPyPzg",821,1041,"hazard/counterplay","Against a staged Hazard, a visible damage threat can bait his jump; if the target survives, teammates can move past his position and punish him later or pressure the backline.","conditional_rule","Sojourn bait examples; team has escape and sustain","high","high","Speaker's narrated outcomes, not verified fight results."),
 ("P4-117","QvMsOy1wFr4",1,211,"composition/ultimate_economy","He evaluates a composition matchup separately in neutral and ultimate fights: the Sombra–Queen team seeks a slow, baiting neutral that preserves its fragile damage dealers and farms toward powerful ultimates.","framework","NRG versus Mauga composition in 2024","high","high","Contextual counterexample to a blanket dismissal of ultimate economy; patch-specific."),
 ("P4-118","QvMsOy1wFr4",212,391,"turns/pressure","An engaging composition can use an early turn to force major cooldowns and space, briefly reset, then use a later third or fifth turn to finish once the opponent has fewer answers.","conditional_rule","Mauga versus Sombra–Queen neutral; ult availability matters","high","high","A full overpowering first turn is another stated option when setup and ultimates allow it."),
 ("P4-119","QvMsOy1wFr4",802,1003,"composition/engage","An engaging team can stage its durable threats where clearing them exposes the opponent to the engage; a defender may need to clear together along another route.","mechanism","NRG Midtown example; engagement role shifts with ultimates","high","high","He praises setup despite that particular fight loss; do not infer the plan guaranteed a win."),
 ("P4-120","QvMsOy1wFr4",1003,1395,"composition/counterplay","Against a backline that baits an engage and a frontline that blocks access, the rush can first pressure the frontline and force protective cooldowns; that either exposes the frontline or brings the backline close enough to reach.","conditional_rule","NRG Queen–Venture–Genji versus Toronto Zarya composition","high","high","Counterplay is matchup and path dependent; another possible outcome is discussed in the source."),
 ("P4-121","QvMsOy1wFr4",1395,1704,"ultimate_economy/corner","On retake into Graviton, staying off the contested corner can create room to bait or answer the ultimate; grouping on the corner removes the escape and trade options even after a sound neutral.","case_judgment","NRG–Toronto examples; specific ult deficit","high","high","Narrated fight diagnosis needs visual review; preserves ultimate-based counterexample."),
 ("P4-122","STbH6hH8emk",683,889,"echo/copy","After an early Echo copy, check whether opponents can turn and burst it; if they can, fall back to a longer frontline fight, while a committed opposing frontline may permit a backline reach.","conditional_rule","Reaper copies in Mauga–Echo mirror","high","high","Requires POV and cooldown verification."),
 ("P4-123","XhcF5IzJDq4",535,916,"support/exposure","In this Brigitte brawl meta, time spent close to one's own frontline raises the risk of being caught by the next fast engage; cycle out after a trigger rather than remain for another whip or heal attempt.","conditional_rule","2024 Mauga–Brigitte examples","high","high","The speaker's 'unluckiness meter' is a metaphor, not a quantified probability; context narrower than all Brigitte play."),
 ("P4-124","XhcF5IzJDq4",914,1065,"support/trade","After gaining a pick, a Brigitte may preserve the advantage by staying difficult to trade, rather than moving up merely because the team is ahead.","case_judgment","Specific five-versus-four brawl example","high","high","Inspect who could actually reach the support in the replay."),
 ("P4-125","K6Ayz-NHVe4",773,1006,"bait/counterplay","Against a bait setup, clear or poke the players taking attention before chasing the distant backline; this can force movement cooldowns and remove their ability to keep baiting.","conditional_rule","Falcons–Nightmare Mauga composition examples","high","high","Speaker's regional comparison is rhetoric, not evidence of universal regional skill."),
 ("P4-126","K6Ayz-NHVe4",1006,1183,"bait/advantage","After gaining a pick while pressing a bait setup, durable threats can advance while vulnerable backliners keep their offset positions, preserving answers to a counter-engage.","conditional_rule","Falcons–Nightmare example","high","high","Visual audit needed for actual player positions."),
 ("P4-127","V-Y0hBOI1yY",374,525,"tank/ammo","In a Mauga mirror, reload behind a corner before committing to the midfight, even at the cost of some poke damage, because running out of ammunition also removes sustain during the exchange.","conditional_rule","2024 Mauga mirror and then-current kit","high","medium","Mechanics and exact resource balance are patch dependent."),
 ("P4-128","V-Y0hBOI1yY",743,953,"tank/ultimate","Cage placement should fit the follow-up ultimate and avoid sacrificing armor to catch more targets; the best enclosure for a Reaper follow-up can differ from one supporting a copy or a rally.","conditional_rule","2024 Mauga brawl examples","high","high","Specific combos and target geometry await footage."),
 ("P4-129","nddeTxFzT6Q",168,344,"hitscan/mechanics","Against predictable tank movement, he recommends keeping the crosshair at head level and using one's own strafe to align shots, instead of relying on repeated large mouse corrections.","method","Hitscan aiming illustration; no measured rank comparison","medium","high","The captions are translation-like and garbled; verify audio and footage before endorsing mechanics claims."),
 ("P4-130","nddeTxFzT6Q",344,520,"hitscan/safety","A hitscan staying hard to reach must still deal enough damage to relieve frontline pressure; hiding safely without threatening the enemy defeats the role's purpose.","distinction","Corner and Orisa examples","medium","high","ASR wording needs audio verification; connects P4-044 and P4-045."),
 ("P4-131","nddeTxFzT6Q",728,960,"hitscan/midfight","A hitscan can keep firing through a long fight from an offset position, but should withdraw as soon as the frontline protection is cleared or enemy movement signals a reach, before taking damage.","conditional_rule","Specific Sojourn examples; tank or Brigitte may be the temporary cover","medium","high","Player POV and chronology need visual check."),
 ("P4-132","E1bYy6OE_OQ",321,505,"information/setup","Between fights, seek safe sight of likely enemy setup locations before withdrawing to the real defensive position; an unseen attacker can finish staging while the team has no timely response.","conditional_rule","GK–Liquid examples; avoid dying during forward scouting","high","high","The visibility claims require each player's POV; speaker explicitly warns against overextending."),
 ("P4-133","LpxT2dykNK0",219,438,"space/counterplay","When an engaging team takes space toward a strong setup, the defending team has a short window to contest that setup with its cooldowns or an ultimate; yielding continuously can make the later engage difficult to answer.","conditional_rule","Two 2025 match examples; depends on which setup is becoming strong","high","high","Read with P4-031: early deliberate withdrawal with a new route differs from allowing a threatening setup to finish."),
 ("P4-134","MYW1ztAeDQc",761,929,"dive/prevention","If attackers' DPS angles and Winston's forward position are about to make a dive strong, a defender can spend an ultimate proactively to clear the setup, rather than save it for surviving the completed dive.","conditional_rule","Defending a retake in a large ultimate fight","high","high","The video uses absolute rhetoric about good dives; the proposed ult timing is conditional and needs footage."),
 ("P4-135","1UNctVbRS3M",520,704,"dive/staging","When the opponent withdraws to reload or recover, the same moment can let a dive player disappear from sight and take a new route before the next exchange.","mechanism","Ball–Genji low-damage dive example","high","high","Specific sight lines and whether the opponent truly lost track need POV review."),
 ("P4-136","1UNctVbRS3M",704,900,"dive/communication","If an enemy clearing a flank cannot quickly turn onto the rest of the team, the flanker can call for teammates to act; if the clearer can immediately turn onto them, the team should often wait and restage.","conditional_rule","Diving team with one player pressured on an angle","high","high","Exact turn distance and crossfire are visual judgments."),
 ("P4-137","1UNctVbRS3M",900,1069,"dive/commitment","An early soft dive can force cooldowns and reveal a rotation without a wide hard pinch; the degree of split and commitment should match whether the team actually intends to finish the fight.","conditional_rule","Ball–Genji spawn defense versus defensive ultimates","high","high","Specific fight result and route need replay validation."),
 ("P4-138","1UNctVbRS3M",1069,1255,"dive/pathing","Against a tank who can stuff the direct route, bait the tank toward a less valuable path and move around during the opening; a fast composition need not hard commit on its first engage.","conditional_rule","Low-damage Ball–Genji composition against Ramattra","high","high","Map geometry and the tank's options require visual audit."),
 ("P4-139","1UNctVbRS3M",1255,1494,"dive/trigger","A dive team can actively create its trigger by pressuring an opposing tank until it withdraws to recover, while denying the enemy damage dealers their setup; the tank's retreat then opens a coordinated backline dive.","mechanism","Ball–Genji defense against D.Va","high","high","Narrated cooldown and armor states are unverified."),
 ("P4-140","jSCHyAWoUjc",94,181,"dps/attention","An initiating flex DPS should leave or defend when multiple opponents turn to look at them, instead of waiting for low health; drawing attention without taking the resulting damage can already create value.","conditional_rule","Vendetta review; early flank and cooldown bait","high","high","The claimed gaze and timing require POV review; do not read as never taking damage."),
 ("P4-141","jSCHyAWoUjc",604,758,"dps/staging","A DPS can poke from a powerful forward position between fights, then leave before the opponent reaches a clearing position; a flexible second position permits scouting and later re-entry.","conditional_rule","Vendetta defense with pre-fight time","high","high","Depends on map routes and opponent clear; speaker exempts spawn/stagger cases."),
 ("P4-142","jSCHyAWoUjc",758,973,"dps/bait","When an opponent is baiting an engage, retaining the movement cooldown while walking or threatening can force their escape first, allowing the later engage to punish that spent resource.","conditional_rule","Vendetta against Sojourn slide, then ultimate threat","high","high","Specific cooldown sequence needs replay; do not generalize to all matchups."),
 ("P4-143","M8393UkZxjY",357,599,"composition/split_timing","In a retake, assigning the right heroes to each split is insufficient if both groups show early and can be marked together; establish or occupy space first, then split where the opponent cannot readily control both groups.","conditional_rule","Team Liquid–Falcons review; Ramattra/Sojourn/Genji example","medium","high","Caption rendering is translation-like; exact routes and criticism await footage."),
 ("P4-144","M8393UkZxjY",599,790,"composition/aggro_balance","A split should decide which group takes attention first and give it enough resources; exposing both groups at once can leave both under pressure without a useful counterattack.","mechanism","Same 2025 retake; composition and ult state matter","medium","high","Connects 2023 push/pull and 2026 aggro balance, without assuming identical compositions."),
 ("P4-145","M8393UkZxjY",1139,1359,"dive/setup","Before a nano dive, supports may need to help a DPS establish a useful angle so the damage line can join the tank's entry; a solo tank dive with teammates blocked from sight yields little follow-up.","case_judgment","Liquid–Falcons watch-party example","medium","high","Narrated player positions need POV confirmation; several alternative routes were proposed."),
 ("P4-146","M8393UkZxjY",1359,1529,"dive/marking","He diagnoses the reviewed team's dive as too easy to mark: opponents can pressure the tank, damage dealers, and supports at once because no group establishes a protected angle or distracts for the others.","case_judgment","Liquid–Falcons watch-party summary","medium","high","This is his team evaluation, not independent measurement of five simultaneous marks."),
 ("P4-147","t1dnez3yuZ4",130,357,"ultimate_economy/sequence","In an ultimate fight, layering defensive resources in response to separate threats can preserve an ultimate for the chase or next turn; spending Rush, Beat, and Bob together on the same kite may waste options.","case_judgment","SSG–Crazy Raccoon watch party","medium","high","Narrated sequencing and alternative outcomes require video review."),
 ("P4-148","Y4ORvoqZ1P0",422,606,"dps/matchup","A Freya facing a Symmetra teleport rush must stage near a route back to support and keep her escape available; a poke angle inside teleport reach is punishable even if the first attack misses.","conditional_rule","Specific 2025 hero matchup","high","high","Patch and map dependent; speaker revises judgments on some later fights."),
 ("P4-149","sqtmsbHxrLE",1,197,"draft/preparation","Scrim bans can serve long-term matchup practice, while imminent tournament preparation should rehearse bans and map picks that maximize the chance of winning the actual match.","distinction","Ban-era tournament commentary; regional examples are anecdotal","high","low","Do not treat regional scrim or match performance assertions as verified from transcript alone."),
 ("P4-150","sqtmsbHxrLE",674,1000,"execution/attention","Knowing a matchup interaction in review does not ensure it is executed under match pressure; the speaker describes both freezing after an advantage and rushing forward impulsively as ways attention can fail.","framework","Winston–Lucio boop example and coaching reflection","high","medium","Claims about particular players' nervousness are speculative; preserve as general coaching hypothesis."),
 ("P4-151","LSrm0ocaS1Q",182,338,"hitscan/aiming","He analyzes aiming as predicting a target's likely strafe change after they notice a threat, sometimes waiting with the crosshair ahead of that movement rather than chasing every step.","method","Specific hitscan POV; speaker states player intention is a guess","high","high","Aims and inferred intention require footage; probabilities are qualitative."),
 ("P4-152","LSrm0ocaS1Q",830,1029,"hitscan/aiming","After landing a shot, briefly holding a well-placed crosshair can catch a target's return strafe; the choice to follow or cut off depends on the observed short or long strafe pattern.","conditional_rule","Hitscan clip analysis","high","high","Speaker's interpretation of aim technique, not a measured mechanical advantage."),
 ("P4-153","AcAxvnAEYpg",1,184,"retake/walk_up","Against an early dive hit, a retaking group can choose a route where the hit has little backline follow-up, survive it, and only then advance to objective with useful angles.","conditional_rule","SSG–Liquid Ball defense on Ilios","high","high","Path, timing, and denied sight lines require match POV review."),
 ("P4-154","AcAxvnAEYpg",184,360,"retake/counterplay","If a defending group is strong inside a room but must eventually leave to touch objective, a dive team can threaten the exit instead of forcing a weak entry into the room.","conditional_rule","Specific point and composition; objective clock permits waiting","high","high","Visual geometry and actual contest timing need validation."),
 ("P4-155","AcAxvnAEYpg",362,712,"roles/turns","A frontline's first move does not automatically authorize the backline to follow; supports and damage dealers may need to keep their safer angle until distance, cooldowns, and space permit their own turn.","conditional_rule","SSG–Liquid retake and Lucio examples","high","high","Speaker's judgments about individual deaths need replay review."),
 ("P4-156","1OvQ5PAK0w0",326,691,"attention/reset","A lull or reset in a fight is a chance to stop focusing on the prior target, reassess ultimates and the next objective touch, and protect attention for the next threat; noticing the correct plan only in hindsight is insufficient.","method","2025 pro review; mental state inference","high","medium","Player thoughts are the speaker's hypothesis, not observed internal facts."),
 ("P4-157","1OvQ5PAK0w0",691,873,"attention/scanning","A tank reloading behind cover can use the moment to check whether the backline is occupied by a flanker before committing forward, rather than assuming teammates' calls will provide all relevant information.","conditional_rule","Specific Zarya point contest","high","high","Exact sight and timing need POV; the percentage of mental bandwidth in speech is illustrative."),
 ("P4-158","1OvQ5PAK0w0",873,1052,"ultimate_economy/tempo","If two useful ultimates are nearly charged, the team can delay stepping onto point long enough to farm them while addressing a known flank; an early point walk can lose control of the fight before the planned tools arrive.","case_judgment","Nightmare match example; objective time available","high","high","Conditional counterexample to treating ultimate count as irrelevant; verify charge and clock visually."),
 ("P4-159","2X_yEWyNms0",212,391,"game_design/roles","His balance philosophy favors keeping broad play styles such as hitscan and ground tank viable so players have adjacent hero options, while situational heroes should remain situational rather than dominate every map.","design_opinion","Opinion on a specific 2025 patch, not empirical balance ranking","high","low","The named tiers and strength judgments are time and patch dependent."),
 ("P4-160","2X_yEWyNms0",390,618,"game_design/balance","He proposes strengthening a weak role first, tuning overperforming members within it, and revisiting older heroes whose tools no longer serve their intended 5v5 interactions.","design_opinion","His proposed balance sequence; not a tested intervention","high","low","Preserve as design preference, including his admitted simplification."),
 ("P4-161","TOaKp3Z44ho",746,873,"retake/pathing","If a retake requires control of a side of the map, send enough of the team along that route to establish it; a small unsupported DPS–Lucio split can be cleared before it creates useful pressure.","conditional_rule","Specific Lijiang retake; tank shows elsewhere","high","high","The absolute language is rhetoric; map and enemy setup determine viable allocations."),
 ("P4-162","ln2t2rl1KYw",236,421,"space/engage_range","He calls the region where an opponent can initiate an effective hit the 'pocket'; entering it before the team has chosen its route and is ready to fight can force valuable cooldowns merely to survive.","definition","Specific Flashpoint retake examples; boundary varies by map and setup","high","high","The pocket is a qualitative threat area, not a fixed distance; inspect actual reach."),
 ("P4-163","ln2t2rl1KYw",421,778,"space/pathing","Path and scout outside the opponent's effective engage range, then cross it together when the team can use its cooldowns for space or a fight rather than losing them during an unplanned walk-up.","conditional_rule","2025 low-range compositions; examples include baiting the first hit","high","high","Exact sight lines and cooldown states require replay."),
 ("P4-164","ln2t2rl1KYw",1059,1367,"roles/turns","A Genji or Lucio should enter a dangerous objective or side-lane fight when a touch, follow-up, or chosen map-control goal calls for it; a teammate fighting there does not alone make immediate participation valuable.","conditional_rule","Specific Flashpoint fights and coaching analogy","high","high","Not a categorical ban on helping allies or fighting side lanes; speaker expressly qualifies that."),
 ("P4-165","aNBstKtsPms",418,650,"fight_plan/flexibility","A planned early fight should retain a practical retreat route; if an ally is forced out, an enemy flank arrives, or the timing is missed, the team can call a withdrawal without being trapped by its initial plan.","conditional_rule","Reaction to another coach's review; Orisa–Sojourn example","high","medium","Separate Capitology's endorsement from the reviewed coach's speech; exact positions need video."),
 ("P4-166","aNBstKtsPms",650,812,"dps/bait","A vulnerable long-range DPS can sometimes play a threatening but expensive-to-kill position: if opponents devote large resources to reach her, teammates gain space to punish elsewhere.","mechanism","Capitology interpreting a guest's Doom–Widow review","medium","high","Guest attribution and actual resource exchange require audio/video; do not treat dying as inherently valuable."),
 ("P4-167","vu4KmVKp2f0",204,354,"composition/teleport_counterplay","Against a Symmetra teleport composition, pressure the staging route before a strong teleport becomes possible, then be ready to fight an adequate teleport promptly before its new map position yields more value.","conditional_rule","Falcons and Crazy Raccoon examples; composition may affect ability to contest","high","high","Two distinct phases in the speaker's counterplay; exact setup and teleport outcomes need footage."),
